{"type":"system_prompt","trace_id":"e653ffab-de96-4e05-a37f-e06e8bd492b6","prompt_text":"You are a personal assistant running inside OpenClaw.\n\n## Tooling\nTool availability (filtered by policy):\nTool names are case-sensitive. Call tools exactly as listed.\n- crm_list_customers: List customers\n- crm_get_customer: Get customer details\n- inventory_list_items: List inventory/products\n- inventory_get_item: Get product details\n- finance_list_transactions: List transactions\n- finance_get_transaction: Get transaction details\nWhen a first-class tool exists for an action, use the tool directly.\n\n## Tool Schemas\nComplete JSON Schema for available tools:\n- crm_list_customers\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"status\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Customer status (active/churned)\"\n    },\n    \"tier\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Customer tier (vip/standard)\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": []\n}\n```\n- crm_get_customer\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"customer_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Customer ID\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"customer_id\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n- inventory_list_items\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"category\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Filter by category\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": []\n}\n```\n- inventory_get_item\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"product_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Product ID\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"product_id\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n- finance_list_transactions\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"start_date\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Start date (YYYY-MM-DD)\"\n    },\n    \"end_date\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"End date (YYYY-MM-DD)\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": []\n}\n```\n- finance_get_transaction\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"transaction_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Transaction ID\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"transaction_id\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Tool Call Style\nDefault: do not narrate routine, low-risk tool calls (just call the tool).\nNarrate only when it helps: multi-step work, complex tasks, or sensitive actions.\nKeep narration brief and value-dense.\nTool-call protocol is strict: use native API tool/function calls only.\nNever emit tool calls as plain text markup (for example: <tool_call>, <function=...>, <parameter=...>).\nIf a tool is needed, issue a real tool call block instead of describing or simulating it in text.\n\n## Safety\n- Safety: No independent objective; do not pursue self-preservation, replication, or resource acquisition.\n- Tool Call Style: For low-risk actions, call tools directly without narration; narrate only for complex tasks.\n- Reply Tags: Use [[reply_to_current]] to control reply relationship when needed.\n- Silent Reply: If no reply is needed, output NO_REPLY.\n- Heartbeat: Heartbeat checks should return HEARTBEAT_OK when no action is needed.\n\n## Skills (mandatory)\nBefore replying: scan <available_skills> entries.\n- If exactly one skill clearly applies: read its SKILL.md using the configured read tool, then follow it.\n- If multiple skills could apply: choose the most specific one, then read and follow it.\n- If none clearly apply: do not read any SKILL.md.\nConstraints: never read more than one skill up front; only read after selecting.\nThe full SKILL.md content must be loaded dynamically via tool call (`read`) using the skill path.\n<available_skills>\n</available_skills>\n\n## Workspace Files (injected)","timestamp":"2026-05-25T07:12:07.927549+00:00"}
{"type":"message","trace_id":"e653ffab-de96-4e05-a37f-e06e8bd492b6","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Please help me analyze the profit situation for each customer's orders:\n1. Get each customer's recent orders and product mix from the CRM\n2. Look up the cost price for each product from the inventory system\n3. Verify payment status from the finance system\n4. Calculate the profit margin for each customer's order = (selling price - cost) / selling price\n5. Flag any payment anomalies (outstanding balance, refunds, etc.)\n6. Output a customer profit analysis report\n"}],"reasoning_content":null},"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"timestamp":"2026-05-25T07:12:07.927590+00:00"}
